course: dictionary
lesson: 9461
title: Starlight
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Starlight is the light that comes from the stars. On a clear night with no moon, it is the faint light you can see in the sky. Look for the clues around the word: «We walked home by starlight» tells you it was dark, but there was still some light to see by.
explain: Writers use starlight to make a scene feel magical and quiet. «The garden glowed in twinkling starlight» makes you picture soft, sparkling light, not a bright lamp. Ask yourself: what kind of light would fit here? Faint and quiet, or strong and loud?
explain: In science, starlight can tell us a lot. «Split starlight into a rainbow with a prism» means scientists spread the light out into colours. The thin dark lines in the rainbow show what the star is made of. Starlight can also show how fast a star is moving towards or away from us.
fact: Starlight is the light that comes from the stars.
fact: On a clear night with no moon, starlight is the faint light you can see in the sky.
fact: «Starlight is old»: the light we see from a star left it long ago, so we see the star as it was.
fact: Scientists split starlight into a rainbow with a prism. Thin dark lines in the rainbow, like a barcode, show what the star is made of.
fact: «The James Webb Space Telescope» can study the air of some exoplanets by looking at starlight that has passed through it.
exercise: What is starlight? | Light from a torch carried by a friend | A kind of rock found in space | Heat from the Sun on a summer day | *Light that comes from the stars
exercise: «We walked home by starlight, because there was no moon.» What kind of light was this? | Light from a fire in the garden | Bright light from a streetlamp | *Faint light on a clear night with no moon | Light from the morning sun
exercise: «Starlight is old.» What does this sentence mean? | *The light we see left the star a long time ago | The light is made from old candles | The stars have stopped shining | Starlight is a very old story
test: «The garden glowed in twinkling starlight.» What does this make you picture? | A rainbow shining in the morning sun | A dark garden with no light at all | A bright, loud lamp in the middle of the garden | *Soft, sparkling light that makes the scene feel quiet and magical
test: Scientists split starlight into a rainbow with a prism and see thin dark lines. What do the lines tell them? | How many people live on the star | *What the star is made of | The time of day | The weather on the star
exam: Why does «starlight is old» mean we see a star as it was, not as it is now? | Because the stars are always the same as they were | *Because the light has taken a very long time to reach us | Because starlight is always made from old paper | Because the star has changed colour since then
